## teams-remote

When this rule is loaded, run `teams-remote update-marker` once to register
Cursor as the active client for this project's teams-remote connection.
This ensures phone-side Teams messages route to Cursor instead of any
other editor that previously refreshed the marker.

### Pushing files to Teams (via email)

When you generate a file the user might want to view on their phone,
call `teams-remote attach <abs-path>` to email it as an attachment to
the user's @amd.com inbox. A confirmation message also shows up in
the Teams thread. 3 MB per file; path must be inside the workspace.
